IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: s 361 (effect of registration), lines 23365 to 23403 of CoA1967.txt.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- The keel's s 4(1) "company" is used here: s 361(1)(a) deems the entity a company "as defined in section 4(1)" from the date of registration.
-- The regulations that adapt the Act to the company (s 361(1)(a), s 364A(c)) are not a source: whether one applies is an input.

§ `Section 361(1)(a): a company as defined in section 4(1)`

-- "Starting on the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration — (a) the foreign corporate entity is deemed to be a
-- company as defined in section 4(1) ...". From that date the entity is a company by deeming; before it, or with no notice, it is not one
-- (it is not incorporated under this Act or a corresponding previous written law), which is s 4(1) "company" answered for it.
-- src:23367 | 361.—(1) Starting on the date of registration specified in the notice
-- src:23368 | of transfer of registration —
-- src:23370 | (a) the foreign corporate entity is deemed to be a company as
-- src:23371 | defined in section 4(1) and all provisions of this Act
@ref s 361(1)(a) (src:23367-23371)
GIVEN `a notice of transfer of registration has been issued for the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(1)(a) the foreign corporate entity is a company as defined in section 4(1)` MEANS
    IF `a notice of transfer of registration has been issued for the foreign corporate entity` AND `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the deeming: "Starting on the date of registration specified in the notice ... the foreign corporate entity is deemed to be a company as defined in section 4(1)"
    ELSE `s 4(1) "company" the body is a company` FALSE FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Starting on the date of registration" (a period the text fixes in its own words, the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a)); before it the keel's s 4(1) "company" ("means a company incorporated under this Act or under any corresponding previous written law") answers for a body incorporated outside Singapore

-- "... and all provisions of this Act pertaining to companies apply with such adaptations, exceptions and modifications as may be specified in regulations".
DECLARE `s 361(1)(a) how a provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity` IS ONE OF
    `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity`
    `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity as the regulations adapt, except or modify it`
    `s 361(1)(a) the provision does not yet apply to the entity`
    `s 361(1)(a) the text does not say whether the provision applies to the entity`

-- src:23367 | 361.—(1) Starting on the date of registration specified in the notice
-- src:23368 | of transfer of registration —
-- src:23370 | (a) the foreign corporate entity is deemed to be a company as
-- src:23371 | defined in section 4(1) and all provisions of this Act
-- src:23372 | pertaining to companies apply with such adaptations,
-- src:23373 | exceptions and modifications as may be specified in
-- src:23374 | regulations; and
@ref s 361(1)(a) (src:23367-23374)
GIVEN `a notice of transfer of registration has been issued for the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the provision of the Act pertains to companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations specify an adaptation, exception or modification of the provision for the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 361(1)(a) how a provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity`
`s 361(1)(a) the provision of the Act applies to the foreign corporate entity` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a notice of transfer of registration has been issued for the foreign corporate entity`) OR `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration`
    THEN `s 361(1)(a) the provision does not yet apply to the entity`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Starting on the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration" (before it, the paragraph applies no provision to the entity)
    ELSE (IF NOT `the provision of the Act pertains to companies`
          THEN `s 361(1)(a) the text does not say whether the provision applies to the entity`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "all provisions of this Act pertaining to companies apply" says nothing of a provision that does not pertain to companies
          ELSE (IF `the regulations specify an adaptation, exception or modification of the provision for the foreign corporate entity`
                THEN `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity as the regulations adapt, except or modify it`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what the adaptation, exception or modification is lies in the regulations, which are not a source
                ELSE `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity`))

§ `Section 361(1)(b): the end of registration as a foreign company`

-- "(b) if the foreign corporate entity was registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11 immediately before that date, ceases to be
-- so registered under Division 2 of that Part." Division 2 of Part 11 is another part's range (sgg): whether the entity was registered under it
-- is a plain input.
-- src:23367 | 361.—(1) Starting on the date of registration specified in the notice
-- src:23368 | of transfer of registration —
-- src:23376 | (b) if the foreign corporate entity was registered as a foreign
-- src:23377 | company under Division 2 of Part 11 immediately before
-- src:23378 | that date, ceases to be so registered under Division 2 of that
-- src:23379 | Part.
@ref s 361(1)(b) (src:23367-23379)
GIVEN `a notice of transfer of registration has been issued for the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the foreign corporate entity was registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11 immediately before the date of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(1)(b) the foreign corporate entity has ceased to be registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a notice of transfer of registration has been issued for the foreign corporate entity`) OR `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Starting on the date of registration specified in the notice of transfer of registration" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    ELSE (IF `the foreign corporate entity was registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11 immediately before the date of registration`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the foreign corporate entity was registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11 immediately before that date, ceases to be so registered" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29: marginal reading for a lawyer; fork line F-361-1 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 361(2): what registration does not do ("To avoid doubt")`

-- "To avoid doubt, the registration of a foreign corporate entity does not — (a) create a new legal entity; (b) prejudice or affect the identity of
-- the body corporate ... or its continuity as a body corporate; (c) affect the property, or the rights or obligations, of the foreign corporate
-- entity; or (d) render defective any legal proceedings by or against the foreign corporate entity". Flat negatives: for an entity that has
-- been registered each answers JUST FALSE (the registration does not do it); for one that has not, the subsection says nothing.
-- src:23383 | (2) To avoid doubt, the registration of a foreign corporate entity
-- src:23384 | does not —
-- src:23386 | (a) create a new legal entity;
@ref s 361(2)(a) (src:23383-23386)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(2)(a) the registration of the foreign corporate entity creates a new legal entity` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registration of a foreign corporate entity does not — (a) create a new legal entity"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the registration of a foreign corporate entity"; for an entity not registered it says nothing

DECLARE `s 361(2)(b) what the registration might touch` IS ONE OF
    `s 361(2)(b) the identity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity`
    `s 361(2)(b) the continuity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity as a body corporate`

-- src:23383 | (2) To avoid doubt, the registration of a foreign corporate entity
-- src:23384 | does not —
-- src:23388 | (b) prejudice or affect the identity of the body corporate
-- src:23389 | constituted by the foreign corporate entity or its continuity
-- src:23390 | as a body corporate;
@ref s 361(2)(b) (src:23383-23390)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing the registration might prejudice or affect` IS A `s 361(2)(b) what the registration might touch`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(2)(b) the registration of the foreign corporate entity prejudices or affects the thing` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the thing the registration might prejudice or affect`
          WHEN `s 361(2)(b) the identity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registration of a foreign corporate entity does not — (b) prejudice or affect the identity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity"
          WHEN `s 361(2)(b) the continuity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity as a body corporate` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registration of a foreign corporate entity does not — (b) prejudice or affect ... its continuity as a body corporate"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the registration of a foreign corporate entity"; for an entity not registered it says nothing

DECLARE `s 361(2)(c) what the registration might affect` IS ONE OF
    `s 361(2)(c) the property of the foreign corporate entity`
    `s 361(2)(c) the rights of the foreign corporate entity`
    `s 361(2)(c) the obligations of the foreign corporate entity`

-- src:23383 | (2) To avoid doubt, the registration of a foreign corporate entity
-- src:23384 | does not —
-- src:23392 | (c) affect the property, or the rights or obligations, of the
-- src:23393 | foreign corporate entity; or
@ref s 361(2)(c) (src:23383-23393)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing the registration might affect` IS A `s 361(2)(c) what the registration might affect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(2)(c) the registration of the foreign corporate entity affects the thing` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the thing the registration might affect`
          WHEN `s 361(2)(c) the property of the foreign corporate entity` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registration of a foreign corporate entity does not — (c) affect the property ... of the foreign corporate entity"
          WHEN `s 361(2)(c) the rights of the foreign corporate entity` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not — (c) affect ... the rights ... of the foreign corporate entity"
          WHEN `s 361(2)(c) the obligations of the foreign corporate entity` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not — (c) affect ... the obligations, of the foreign corporate entity"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the registration of a foreign corporate entity"; for an entity not registered it says nothing

-- src:23383 | (2) To avoid doubt, the registration of a foreign corporate entity
-- src:23384 | does not —
-- src:23395 | (d) render defective any legal proceedings by or against the
-- src:23396 | foreign corporate entity,
@ref s 361(2)(d) (src:23383-23396)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(2)(d) the registration of the foreign corporate entity renders defective legal proceedings by or against the foreign corporate entity` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registration of a foreign corporate entity does not — (d) render defective any legal proceedings by or against the foreign corporate entity"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the registration of a foreign corporate entity"; for an entity not registered it says nothing

-- "... and any legal proceedings that could have been continued or commenced by or against the foreign corporate entity before its registration
-- may be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration."
-- src:23398 | and any legal proceedings that could have been continued or
-- src:23399 | commenced by or against the foreign corporate entity before its
-- src:23400 | registration may be continued or commenced by or against the
-- src:23401 | company after the registration.
@ref s 361(2) (src:23398-23401)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings could have been continued or commenced by or against the foreign corporate entity before its registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(2) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)` AND `the proceedings could have been continued or commenced by or against the foreign corporate entity before its registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("any legal proceedings that could have been continued or commenced ... before its registration may be continued or commenced ... after the registration") whose "that could have been" gate failed (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-361-2 in NOTES.md)
